      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 7489,
        "name": "Nibelung",
        "desc": "<p>The leader of the elemental dragons and the primeval creator of Teyvat.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2025/03/03/237301566/596896f7ea3d51d7b1f6e504094f9d97_4010709984094972573.png",
        "displayStyle": "card",
        "menuId": 10
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": "The primeval dragon created three Moon Goddesses and the Three Moons, and raised them to the sky. During the",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 9095,
        "name": "War of Funerary Flame",
        "desc": "<p>The war between the Dragon Lord Nibelung and the Heavenly Principles that took place 6,000 years ago.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2026/01/21/237301566/693da8a1b01352fde999598e49b34fde_8792145013995754059.png",
        "displayStyle": "text"
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": "Nibelung imprisoned the Moon Goddesses and turned their Moons into weapons.",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 7625,
        "name": "Moon Goddesses",
        "desc": "<p>Aria, Sonnet, and Canon — three sisters and Moon Goddesses who once ruled the firmament. Columbina Hyposelenia is a Moon Goddess who was born thousands of years after the Three Moon's death.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2025/04/07/237301566/1f76253cb02cf46c0f6d8b836271b6f2_7450418426638299855.png",
        "displayStyle": "card",
        "menuId": 23
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": "Canon was the Goddess of the Frost Moon — the second and brightest of the Moons. Her glow became the cold, undying lantern of the night. The Frost Moon is the only one that wasn't destroyed during the",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 9095,
        "name": "War of Funerary Flame",
        "desc": "<p>The war between the Dragon Lord Nibelung and the Heavenly Principles that took place 6,000 years ago.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2026/01/21/237301566/693da8a1b01352fde999598e49b34fde_8792145013995754059.png",
        "displayStyle": "text"
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": ".",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 9338,
        "name": "Aria",
        "desc": "<p>Goddess of the Eternal Moon.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2026/01/20/237301566/a2acc52e0870cb103da56037249720e4_9196180589245173426.png",
        "displayStyle": "card"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 9339,
        "name": "Sonnet",
        "desc": "<p>The Goddess of the Iridescent Moon.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2026/01/20/237301566/60ceaba0c8911e94ed390a1c10e39c67_8833187668476967228.png",
        "displayStyle": "card"
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": "Canon is the middle sister.",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 7476,
        "name": "Columbina",
        "desc": "<p>The Trilune Goddess and the former Third of the Eleven Fatui Harbingers, known as Damselette. Her real name is Columbina Hyposelenia.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2026/02/15/237301566/5e2419a3a72fa7e5e3b9f9009281dbbb_5980869753315871646.png",
        "displayStyle": "card",
        "menuId": 10
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": "The new Moon Goddess. Aria, Sonnet, and Canon gave her their powers, thus making her the Trilune Goddess.",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 7622,
        "name": "Frostmoon Scions",
        "desc": "<p>The descendants of the legendary golden realm, who chose to find new homes among the mountains and forests after abandoning all civilization. The only thing they never forsook was their faith in the \"Moon Goddess.\"</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2025/04/07/237301566/495bf3319bc3e1faf3bafaa0ee422e48_5985225249435740207.png",
        "displayStyle": "card",
        "menuId": 23
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": "When",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 4897,
        "name": "Heavenly Principles",
        "desc": "<p>The First Descender, who defeated seven Dragon Sovereigns of the world and created people. The Primordial One may be Phanes.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2024/10/08/237301566/513d51e0ebfd54f5da34a9f85dfaf61f_6047094467838473554.png",
        "displayStyle": "text",
        "menuId": 10
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": "destroyed human civilizations, including",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 8939,
        "desc": "",
        "displayStyle": "text",
        "menuId": 22
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": ", Canon answered the prayers and led the survivors to",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 8826,
        "name": "Hiisi Island",
        "desc": "<p>A mysterious island shrouded in ancient forests, where worship of the Moon Goddess endures. Legends tell of the golden realm's descendants who, guided by moonlight, journeyed countless miles to finally find refuge on these shores.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://act-upload.hoyoverse.com/event-ugc-hoyowiki/2025/09/23/237301566/78a8e1dd1bd89bf1cc3a54aaf005406f_5703030621333879478.png",
        "displayStyle": "text",
        "menuId": 20
      },
      {
        "type": "RichText",
        "text": ". They called the Goddess of the Frost Moon Huurrekuutar, and they took upon the name Frostmoon Scions to honor her further.",
        "alignment": "center"
      },
